# Domain tests and ESLint

When adding, changing, or removing behavior, update tests in the same domain, then run that domain's suite before finishing. Cover the new path and nearby edges (tags, grouping, amounts, dates). Docs-only edits do not need a test run.

Before finishing any implementation, including work done from a plan, run ESLint for every domain the change touches and fix the errors it reports. A plan-file-only edit does not need a lint run. If a touched package has no ESLint config, skip lint for that package and say so.

| Touched paths | Command |
|---|---|
| `src/**` | `CI=true npm test` (`vitest run`; do not pass `--watchAll=false`) |
| `functions/**` | `npm test --prefix functions` |
| `firestore.rules` / `tests/firestore.rules.test.js` | `npm run test:rules` |
| `infra/terraform/**` | `terraform fmt -check` and `terraform validate` in `infra/terraform` |

A change that spans domains runs each matching test and ESLint command. Do not skip existing tests. Do not call live Firebase, Gmail, or Gemini in unit tests.

| Touched paths | ESLint |
|---|---|
| `src/**` | `npm run lint` |
| `functions/**` | `npm run lint --prefix functions` |

- React: grouping, search, budgets, duplicate visibility, merge math, and UI for Duplicate Review / Merge / Tag / Edit Budget / Gmail connect.
- Functions: `detect`, survivor/tag merge, scan filters, Gmail parse, cursor/dedupe, history-404 fallback, invalid_grant. Keep synthetic fixtures in-repo; skip the gitignored dump when missing.
